#! The contextual `then` (s151, wolf-lang#307), through the ONE surface in
#! this repository that can paint it: the server's semantic-token walk.
#!
#! `grammar/if_then_ident.lu` spells `then` four times in three positions —
#! `let then = true` binds it, `if then { … }` reads it as the condition, and
#! `if then then 1 else 0` puts the identifier and the keyword ADJACENT on one
#! line. A regular grammar cannot tell those apart (clients/vscode/inventory.md
#! says so, and is why `then` is CONTEXTUAL rather than a keyword scope), so
#! this transcript is the measurement of what the server actually answers.
#!
#! The whole document first, then line 12 alone as a range request — that is
#! `let n = if then then 1 else 0`, the line where a word-list answer and a
#! position-aware answer differ.
#!
#! WHAT IT MEASURED, at pin a7f517e (v0.2.12), and it was NOT what wolf-lsp#11
#! predicted. The server got the IDENTIFIER half exactly right and emitted
#! NOTHING AT ALL for the keyword half:
#!
#!   L10 C8  `then`  variable  (the binding)
#!   L11 C7  `then`  variable  (the condition)
#!   L12 C15 `then`  variable  (the condition, again)
#!   L12 C20 `then`  — NO TOKEN. `if` at C12 and `else` at C27 were both
#!                    `keyword`; the contextual `then` between them was absent
#!                    from the stream, so an editor painted it as plain text.
#!
#! That was a HOLE, not a miscolouring, and it was the server's: the walk in
#! `crates/wolf_query/src/annotate.rs` tested `AsKw..=WhileKw` and `ThenKw` is
#! declared after that range. Filed as wolf-lang#356; this transcript pinned
#! the defect on purpose so the fix would announce itself as a red here.
#!
#! RE-MEASURED at pin 30731a6 (v0.2.14), which carries the fix (wolf-lang
#! `928f9d9`, s159): the re-record is the one-token diff it was set up to be.
#! Sixteen tokens became SEVENTEEN for the document and five became SIX for the
#! `/range` request over line 12, and the new token in both is
#!
#!   L12 C20 `then`  keyword  (length 4, no modifier)
#!
#! — the same type as the `if` and the `else` beside it. Every identifier
#! `then` is still `variable`; nothing else in either stream moved.
name      annotate/semanticTokens-then
profile   minimal

initialize
open      grammar/if_then_ident.lu
wait      diagnostics grammar/if_then_ident.lu
req       semanticTokens grammar/if_then_ident.lu
req       semanticTokens grammar/if_then_ident.lu 11:0-12:0
shutdown
